    "usage_note": "Matrix values are ABSOLUTE FREQUENCIES of each term in the lowercased, lemmatized full text of the article. Not TF-IDF, not binary presence. The feature space is only these columns, which is why the glossary is the substantive artifact.",
    "marker_split": "quantitative_markers / qualitative_markers / mixed_markers are OURS, not the paper's. The published method feeds all 301 counts to a trained XGBoost model and lets it learn the weights; it never labels a term as leaning one way. These lists were chosen a priori from the methods literature and then validated on six papers, and they exist so a lexical lean can be computed with no model at all. They are DATA rather than code so they can be revised without a release, and a test asserts the Go file and this file agree."
